Package: ssrfr
Type: Package
Title: Server-Side Request Forgery Guard for Outbound Requests
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Bart", "Turczynski", email = "bartek@turczynski.pl", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8788-7980"))
Description: Protects R applications that fetch URLs an attacker can
    influence from server-side request forgery. Each redirect hop is parsed
    once, resolved once, and every resolved address is classified before the
    connection is pinned to a validated address, so a hostname cannot be
    rebound between check and connect. Refusals carry stable reason codes.
    Provides the guarded fetch of each hop of a redirect chain, a helper
    that follows a whole chain, structural inspection of a URL without
    network access, and resolved inspection of every address a name
    resolves to.
